      "output": "The skillful practitioner of the Way is subtle, mysterious, and profoundly penetrating, yet utterly unrecognizable. It is precisely because they are unrecognizable that they cultivate a demeanor of ease and calmness. Like a traveler crossing a river in winter, they appear hesitant and cautious; like fearing one's four neighbors, they remain wary and vigilant. They appear composed as if they were a guest, dispersed as if the ice were melting, and pure as uncarved wood. They are vast as the open sky, and like the valley. They are all-encompassing as if they were turbid. Who can, amid turbidity, quiet it and gradually clarify it? Who can, at rest, endure long movement and gradually bring forth life? The one who preserves this Way does not wish to be full. It is precisely because they are not full that they can endure without needing renewal.",
